{
  "pros": [
    "Consolidates project information, tasks, and communication in one central place",
    "Simplifies breaking down projects into manageable tasks and stages",
    "Provides clear visibility into project status and team responsibilities with efficient task assignment and tracking"
  ],
  "cons": [
    "Search and navigation can become challenging with a large volume of historical data",
    "May lack advanced customization or reporting features found in more complex tools, particularly for date-based progress tracking or approval workflows",
    "Can feel too simplistic for highly intricate projects requiring granular control"
  ],
  "changed": [
    "Changed pro #3: The notes highlighted efficient assignment (autocomplete, chips) and immediate visibility of assignee/due date on the list, making the original 'clear visibility' more specific to how Basecamp achieves it for responsibilities. (Notes: 'Typing 'Sam' in Assigned to gave an autocomplete chip... shows the assignee and due date as compact chips'; 'deliverable showed its assignee and 'Fri, Oct 30' chips on the list right after saving')",
    "Changed con #2: The notes specifically pointed out the lack of a project calendar tool for date-based progress and the absence of approval status/fields, which are specific examples of lacking advanced features. (Notes: 'My Events showed only 'No events today' for October and did not list the to-do due Oct 28, so it was not usable to check project progress by date without a project Calendar tool.'; 'There is no approval status or approval field on to-dos')"
  ]
